  "bump": "minor",
  "title": "@mandate declares its authority as closed moves",
  "summary": "A @mandate may declare an authority section: participant (ref to agent), moves (closed to Observation, Execution, Delegation, Synthesis and Verification), scope (refs to workspaces), excluded-words and covers (path selections). The runtime publishes the mode-to-move table (read, validate, author, effect, re-seat) and mandateRefusal, which the authoring verbs will consume. A mandate without moves restricts no move, a declared moves list names at least one move, and excluded words are refused whatever the moves.",
